    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(2))  # D0..D1\n    units = list(range(4))  # U0..U3\n    supplies = list(range(3))  # S0..S2\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[43.34], [38.98], [21.54]], [[38.86], [41.6], [47.9]], [[16.61], [34.55], [35.81]], [[21.49], [34.68], [46.84]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[88.9], [84.04], [80.04]], [[78.91], [90.22], [112.52]]]\n    transport_costs = [[3.52, 1.67, 2.25, 3.25], [3.13, 1.47, 4.38, 3.01]]\n    risk_costs = [[189.36, 173.26, 150.67, 100.33], [96.17, 155.12, 129.23, 69.68]]\n    supply_volumes = [0.74, 1.29, 0.52]\n    penalty_costs = [65.77, 74.93, 70.99]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA severe coastal storm has disrupted infrastructure across the Riverine Corridor. Access is degraded by washed-out bridges, intermittent landslides, and localized security threats along secondary roads. Supply Depot Alpha (coastal) and Supply Depot Bravo (inland) hold mixed stocks of water, food staples, and medical consumables. Supported elements include Relief Battalion Charlie, Field Hospital Delta, Mobile Clinic Echo, and Displacement Camp Foxtrot, each reporting urgent but varying needs. Weather and daylight constraints limit movement to the current operational period. Security and engineering teams can clear and escort selected ground routes, but doing so consumes scarce enablers and increases exposure.\n\nMission:\nDeliver priority life-sustaining supplies from available depots to supported units within the current operational period, maximizing demand satisfaction while minimizing total operational cost (sum of transport costs, shortage penalties for unmet demand, vehicle deployment costs, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Stocks at each depot are finite; outbound shipments from a depot cannot exceed on-hand supply by item for this period. Transport costs vary by depot-to-unit corridor.\n- Each unit\u2019s demand is a target to be met or exceeded by inbound deliveries across all depots. Controlled shortfalls are permissible only if unavoidable and will incur per-item penalties.\n- Movements are constrained by vehicle capacity measured in volumetric terms relative to each supply type\u2019s loading factor. Dispatching additional vehicles increases cost and consumes limited fleet availability.\n- Routes are activated deliberately. Activating a route (sending any vehicles on that corridor in this period) triggers a fixed Risk Cost to cover escorts, route clearance, and protective overwatch\u2014this cost applies once per route per period, regardless of the number of vehicles subsequently dispatched. Vehicles may only use routes that have been activated.\n- Total vehicle deployments across all corridors are capped by the available fleet for the period. Priority of effort is to sustain medical operations and potable water delivery, then food distribution, balancing transport cost against shortage penalties and fixed route risk.\n- Coordination: Movement Control will sequence convoys to avoid chokepoints; Engineers and Security will confirm route status prior to activation; Depot Operations will stage loads by volume to optimize truck fill; Unit logisticians will confirm receipt windows. All planning parameters are provided in Annex A and will drive the allocation of flows, route activations, and vehicle tasking.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n-----------------------------\nU 0        |  43.34 |  38.98 |  21.54\nU 1        |  38.86 |  41.60 |  47.90\nU 2        |  16.61 |  34.55 |  35.81\nU 3        |  21.49 |  34.68 |  46.84\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n------------------------------\nD 0        |  88.90 |  84.04 |  80.04\nD 1        |  78.91 |  90.22 | 112.52\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |   3.52 |   1.67 |   2.25 |   3.25\nD 1        |   3.13 |   1.47 |   4.38 |   3.01\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        | 189.36 | 173.26 | 150.67 | 100.33\nD 1        |  96.17 | 155.12 | 129.23 |  69.68\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 65.77, Supply S1: 74.93, Supply S2: 70.99]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 0.74, Supply S1: 1.29, Supply S2: 0.52]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nA severe coastal storm has disrupted infrastructure across the Riverine Corridor. Access is degraded by washed-out bridges, intermittent landslides, and localized security threats along secondary roads. Supply Depot Alpha (coastal) and Supply Depot Bravo (inland) hold mixed stocks of water, food staples, and medical consumables. Supported elements include Relief Battalion Charlie, Field Hospital Delta, Mobile Clinic Echo, and Displacement Camp Foxtrot, each reporting urgent but varying needs. Weather and daylight constraints limit movement to the current operational period. Security and engineering teams can clear and escort selected ground routes, but doing so consumes scarce enablers and increases exposure.\n\nMission:\nDeliver priority life-sustaining supplies from available depots to supported units within the current operational period, maximizing demand satisfaction while minimizing total operational cost (sum of transport costs, shortage penalties for unmet demand, vehicle deployment costs, and fixed route security risk costs).\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Stocks at each depot are finite; outbound shipments from a depot cannot exceed on-hand supply by item for this period. Transport costs vary by depot-to-unit corridor.\n- Each unit\u2019s demand is a target to be met or exceeded by inbound deliveries across all depots. Controlled shortfalls are permissible only if unavoidable and will incur per-item penalties.\n- Movements are constrained by vehicle capacity measured in volumetric terms relative to each supply type\u2019s loading factor. Dispatching additional vehicles increases cost and consumes limited fleet availability.\n- Routes are activated deliberately. Activating a route (sending any vehicles on that corridor in this period) triggers a fixed Risk Cost to cover escorts, route clearance, and protective overwatch\u2014this cost applies once per route per period, regardless of the number of vehicles subsequently dispatched. Vehicles may only use routes that have been activated.\n- Total vehicle deployments across all corridors are capped by the available fleet for the period. Priority of effort is to sustain medical operations and potable water delivery, then food distribution, balancing transport cost against shortage penalties and fixed route risk.\n- Coordination: Movement Control will sequence convoys to avoid chokepoints; Engineers and Security will confirm route status prior to activation; Depot Operations will stage loads by volume to optimize truck fill; Unit logisticians will confirm receipt windows. All planning parameters are provided in Annex A and will drive the allocation of flows, route activations, and vehicle tasking.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
